**Read:** [Second Level Course in Heat Transfer — R. P. Vedula](../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF), complete melting/solidification lectures; [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), full applicable transient and phase-change development; [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1), complete relevant phase-equilibrium theory; [FiPy — conservative finite-volume modelling](../sources/FiPy-Conservative-Finite-Volume-Methods.lingua#r_5C155DKGJ5WYGV18EJ1SC41G0Q), complete relevant phase-field/enthalpy examples and their assumptions.

Derive a Stefan balance with an explicit normal and phase convention. Solve a simple similarity problem independently, then compare an enthalpy-based numerical formulation. Recover the total latent-plus-sensible energy account and study the moving-front error under refinement.

Extend to an alloy or a material with a finite transition interval only with an appropriate thermodynamic model. Explain segregation, undercooling or kinetic limitations that prevent an equilibrium phase fraction from determining the complete history. Compare the resulting thermal field with the full metallurgical process question in [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).

Deliver derivations, independently checked limits, numerical evidence and a critical comparison with a complete documented experiment or dataset. Discuss how thermal history, property uncertainty and boundary conditions affect the inferred interface motion and the eventual material, without claiming to have solved microstructure from temperature alone.

**Continue:** [A complete thermal service from physics to continuing use](A-complete-thermal-service-from-physics-to-continuing-use.lingua#r_7J8HFJ2KFHGSRF5EB4JFNRZRB2).

